WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.163
Two more things.

2
00:00:01.163 --> 00:00:03.475
First, a suspected compromise.

3
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:05.917
Learn's page, Secure your Azure Key Vault,

4
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:10.062
says to rotate and migrate dependents
before disabling the old key,

5
00:00:10.062 --> 00:00:14.725
because disabling it first takes
dependent databases and storage offline.

6
00:00:14.725 --> 00:00:16.687
The guide lists that as a danger.

7
00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:20.376
Back up the keys that can't be
recreated, and test a restore.

8
00:00:20.376 --> 00:00:22.425
Second, where agencies are.

9
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:26.789
In commercial Azure, which a G C C
tenant uses, the zone names are the

10
00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:31.638
ones in the commands, such as private
link dot vault core dot azure dot net.

11
00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:33.824
As a side note for Azure Government,

12
00:00:33.824 --> 00:00:37.669
Learn's private endpoint D N S
page gives different zone names,

13
00:00:37.669 --> 00:00:41.515
such as private link dot vault core
dot U S gov cloud A P I dot net,

14
00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:45.587
so any policy that registers
records needs the government names,

15
00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:48.075
and Key Vault's own endpoint differs too.

16
00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:53.323
On other clouds, the guide names Google
Cloud's Private Service Connect,

17
00:00:53.323 --> 00:00:58.900
and O C I private endpoints, a private I
P in a V C N subnet for an Oracle service.
